e-word degree limit.","citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-seed-packets"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"circuit.seed_packets","kind":"claim","label":"Exact small packet and weighted tail estimates","locator":"05-seed-simulation.tex:42–270; lem:seed-packet-estimates, eq:seed-initial-split, eq:seed-exact-special-norm, lem:seed-high-directions","source_id":"circuit-r2-26-source-seed","statement":"Fix small b>0 before r→0. The finite ordinary initialization (cost b/r, mixer arcsin r, inverse cost, mixer π/4) splits exactly into an ordinary component and a special component of norm r. Its high directions ℓ_r,w_r are centered unit vectors, asymptotically orthogonal, and escape every fixed number sector. For bounded number-smooth tails, separated Weyl centers have overlap O(r^M) for every fixed M, while bounded displacements preserve the weighted tail estimates.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.seed_packets","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.seed_packets","id":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22circuit.seed_packets%22%2C%22circuit.ordinary_updates%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22circuit.seed_packets%22%2C%22circuit.ordinary_updates%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.ordinary_updates"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.seed_packets","id":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22circuit.seed_packets%22%2C%22circuit.weighted_unitary_calculus%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"s